### 3. Feedback Source Trade-off Matrix
| Dimension | Exact Verifier (RLVR) | AI Preference Judge (RLAIF) |
| :--- | :--- | :--- |
| **Domain Coverage** | Narrow (requires ground-truth checkers, sandboxes, or unit tests; inapplicable to open-ended dialogue/creative tasks). | Broad (generalizes to open-ended chat, creative writing, nuanced instruction-following without formal oracles). |
| **Label Noise & Variance** | Zero noise (100% deterministic, reproducible, independent of prompt phrasing or response order). | Moderate to High noise (subject to position bias, temperature jitter, and surface prompt heuristics). |
| **Optimization Exploitability** | Outcome-shortcut hacking: rewards lucky or illogical reasoning that stumbles upon the correct designated final token. | Style/fluff hacking: vulnerable to assertive formatting, excessive verbosity, and persuasive filler phrases. |
| **Inference / Training Compute** | Near zero (regex extraction and float comparison execute on CPU in < 1 ms per problem). | High (requires full forward-pass generation over multiple billion parameters per candidate pair or group). |

